    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-duplicate detection for `POST /api/owners` following the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern, keeping structural impact low by adding a new cohesive unit rather than growing any existing method.\n\n**New behaviour (one small function class):**\n- `DetectPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 mirrors the existing `CountNamesakes` step. It runs after the owner is built but before save (so it inspects only pre-existing owners), and flags the new owner `possibleDuplicate=true` / `possibleDuplicateOf=<id>` when another owner shares its last name (case-insensitive) and postcode but has a different telephone; otherwise sets `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n\n**Wiring & plumbing (no existing method bodies changed):**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `detectPossibleDuplicate` step between `countNamesakes` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added two persisted fields with fresh getters/setters (`possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the two read-only fields to the `OwnerDto` schema; MapStruct maps them by name automatically (like `namesakeCount`), so `RespondWithOwner`/`RespondWithOwnerCreated` needed no edits.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `data.sql` \u2014 added the two columns and padded the seed inserts with matching `NULL`s.\n\nThe hard-duplicate paths (`RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`, `RejectDuplicateHousehold`) are untouched, so a genuine duplicate still returns 409 before this step runs; only non-hard-duplicate household matches reach it and are created with the flag set.",
